{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"helpful-stale-wildcat","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context\n\n`templates/rebar-usage.md` currently instructs every project to pass `--assignee <you>`. The claim command already applies `ticket.default_assignee` when the option is omitted. A repository may leave that setting empty, in which case claim remains valid and records no assignee. An explicit value is an override and must be suitable for the configured Jira bridge when one is present. `templates/AGENTS.md` embeds a synchronized generated region from the usage template.\n\n## Plan\n\n- Make the portable claim example omit `--assignee`.\n- Explain the configured default and the valid unassigned result when no default exists.\n- Explain when an explicit Jira-resolvable identity is appropriate without assuming that every client repository uses Jira.\n- Synchronize the generated region in `templates/AGENTS.md` through the established template ownership mechanism.\n- Preserve the existing synchronization test and avoid repository-specific Gerrit guidance in the portable template.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The canonical template presents `rebar claim <id>` as the default command.\n- [ ] The template describes behavior when `ticket.default_assignee` is configured.\n- [ ] The template describes behavior when `ticket.default_assignee` is empty.\n- [ ] Explicit assignee guidance requires a Jira-resolvable identity only when an override is intended.\n- [ ] The generated region in `templates/AGENTS.md` matches `templates/rebar-usage.md`.\n- [ ] The focused template synchronization test passes.","id":"20f3-56b5-6e97-4de3","parent_id":"b8bf-a5aa-2f4d-44d4","priority":1,"tags":["documentation","accuracy","f15"],"ticket_type":"task","title":"F15 correct portable claim identity guidance"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787507522434811001,"uuid":"03c62190-8386-4673-a961-1b15a3261b2e"}